{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","characters":[{"id":"chr_sena_var","name":"Sena Var","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","description":"A junior tide-warden raised among the lock crews, Sena learned to read tide tables from her grandmother and to trust the measured rise against the Glassgate sills. She is lean and sun-browned, with a close-cropped fringe and a habit of keeping chalk marks on her sleeves. Her early surveys were praised for precision, and she has come to treat a clean set of numbers as safer than an uncertain conversation.","motivation":"Keep the lagoon's tide flowing so the city can power its mills and feed its terraces.","goal":"Convince the guilds to pause the glassblowing season long enough for the wardens to dredge the silting locks before the spring tide.","flaw":"She presents evidence as a verdict and dismisses people who need time or trust before they accept it.","internal_conflict":"Sena fears that admitting uncertainty will make the guilds dismiss her warning as inexperience.","external_conflict":"The guilds' long firing calendar clashes with the wardens' need to shut the gates for dredging, while the ferry crews dispute who owns the recovered silt.","arc":"Sena begins convinced that accurate measurements alone should settle the dispute. When a channel-bell check at the locks reveals how the altered tide is already affecting navigation, she chooses to bring the guild and ferry representatives into the survey rather than issue another unilateral warning. She ends still rigorous but willing to share uncertainty and make a common plan before the spring tide.","personality_traits":["observant","earnest","methodical","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tide reading","description":"Compares tide tables, water marks, and the flow through the locks to spot changes in the lagoon's rhythm.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Lock surveying","description":"Measures silt buildup and gate clearance with the tools and procedures used by the Tide Wardens.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_meren_kai","name":"Meren Kai","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","faction_id":"fac_glassblower_guild","description":"Meren is a senior glassblower whose family has held a kiln place at Bellmaker's Quay for three generations. Broad-shouldered and silver-haired, he wears a clear-glass bead from each season he has led and keeps his hands carefully wrapped against kiln heat. He remembers lean years when cancelled work meant empty tables, and sees a full firing calendar as a promise his guild must keep.","motivation":"Protect the guild's livelihood and preserve its standing as keeper of the city's bells and windows.","goal":"Complete the planned glassblowing season without surrendering the guild's chartered work to a premature shutdown.","flaw":"He treats the guild calendar as proof that the season is safe and mistakes compromise for a threat to the guild's authority.","internal_conflict":"Meren fears that yielding to the wardens will make the guild seem unreliable after generations of guarding its craft.","external_conflict":"Sena's warning means the kilns may need to pause while the Glassgate Locks are dredged, disrupting the guild's season and planned commissions.","arc":"Meren begins by refusing to change the firing calendar on a junior warden's report. When a channel bell is found out of tune during the dispute, he must honor the Bell Charter and arrange its recasting within a day; the interruption makes him confront how quickly the silting can threaten the guild's own work. He chooses to shorten the season and help coordinate a pause, ending as a guild leader who can protect the craft by adapting its schedule.","personality_traits":["proud","disciplined","protective","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Glasscraft","description":"Shapes and judges vitrified glass, bells, and floats, recognizing faults that could make them unsafe or out of tune.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Guild negotiation","description":"Can rally artisans around a shared schedule and speak for the guild at the quay.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tavi_ro","name":"Tavi Ro","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative","description":"Tavi captains a sail-and-paddle barge that carries algae harvest, glass, and dredged silt across the lagoon. Compact and strong from years of hauling lines, she wears a patched reed-fiber coat and knots colored cord around her wrist to mark each crew's cargo. She rose from deckhand to captain by making sure her cooperative was paid for difficult work, and is wary of promises that leave the crews bearing the cost.","motivation":"Secure fair recognition and a dependable share for the ferry crews who move the city's harvest and silt.","goal":"Win agreement that dredged silt hauled by the cooperative will be credited to its crews and delivered to the terraces on a clear schedule.","flaw":"She turns every uncertainty into a bargaining position, even when delay puts the whole lagoon at risk.","internal_conflict":"Tavi wants to serve the city that sustains her crew but fears that cooperation will let the wardens take the crew's labor for granted.","external_conflict":"The wardens need the locks dredged before the spring tide, but the cooperative and wardens disagree over the rights and obligations attached to the fertile silt.","arc":"Tavi begins determined to settle the silt-rights dispute before committing her barges. When Sena shows her how little time remains before the spring tide, Tavi chooses to dispatch a barge for the dredging effort while recording the crew's claim and agreeing to spread the silt on the terraces within the season. She ends able to defend her crew's rights without making urgent shared work wait for a perfect bargain.","personality_traits":["resourceful","wary","loyal","direct"],"abilities":[{"name":"Barge handling","description":"Navigates sail-and-paddle barges through lagoon channels and organizes safe cargo movement.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Cargo accounting","description":"Tracks loads, crew labor, and deliveries well enough to challenge unclear claims.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_nima_esh","name":"Nima Esh","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","description":"Nima tends a family plot in the Mangrove Terraces and maintains the silt-traps that protect its rice beds. She is a middle-aged, broad-faced woman with a silver streak in her braid and stained reed gloves tucked into her belt. After her parents lived through the Great Silting, she learned how quickly a clogged lock becomes a hunger, but also how easily arguments over silt can divide neighbors who need one another.","motivation":"Keep the terraces fertile and prevent another season of hunger caused by a failing tide.","goal":"Make sure any silt dredged from the locks reaches the terrace plots in time to benefit the next growing season.","flaw":"She assumes people with formal authority will put their own interests first and sometimes withholds useful knowledge until they prove otherwise.","internal_conflict":"Nima wants the terraces to stand together, yet fears that trusting the guilds or ferry crews will cost her neighbors their share of the silt.","external_conflict":"The wardens, ferry cooperative, and glassblower guild must agree on dredging and its timing, while the terraces depend on both a working tide and the fertile silt.","arc":"Nima begins by guarding her terrace knowledge and expecting the powerful factions to bargain past the growers. When Sena brings the survey to the terraces and Tavi commits a barge to the dredging, Nima chooses to organize growers to prepare the silt-traps and receive the load under the silt-debt rule. She ends as an active broker between the crews and the terraces rather than a wary observer waiting to be overlooked.","personality_traits":["steadfast","practical","protective","slow to trust"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silt-trap tending","description":"Maintains root-garden silt-traps and judges where fertile deposits will best support the terraces.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Grower organizing","description":"Coordinates neighbors around planting, shared labor, and the distribution of terrace resources.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_sena_meren","source_character_id":"chr_sena_var","target_character_id":"chr_meren_kai","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sena Var needs Meren Kai to pause the guild's firing season, while Meren initially doubts her warning and sees her demand as a threat to his guild's livelihood."},{"id":"rel_meren_sena","source_character_id":"chr_meren_kai","target_character_id":"chr_sena_var","relationship_type":"skeptical ally","description":"Meren Kai comes to respect Sena Var's survey after the bell check, but remains protective of the guild's work as they coordinate the pause."},{"id":"rel_sena_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_sena_var","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","relationship_type":"tense ally","description":"Sena Var needs Tavi Ro's barges for dredging; Tavi supports the urgent work but presses Sena to recognize the cooperative's silt claim."},{"id":"rel_tavi_nima","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","target_character_id":"chr_nima_esh","relationship_type":"negotiating partners","description":"Tavi Ro's crews haul the fertile silt that Nima Esh's terraces need, and Nima insists that their agreement fulfill the obligation to spread it within a season."},{"id":"rel_nima_sena","source_character_id":"chr_nima_esh","target_character_id":"chr_sena_var","relationship_type":"cautious ally","description":"Nima Esh helps Sena Var connect the lock emergency to the terraces' needs, while testing whether Sena will include growers in the plan."}]}
