n":"Navigates sail-and-paddle barges through lagoon channels and organizes safe cargo movement.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Cargo accounting","description":"Tracks loads, crew labor, and deliveries well enough to challenge unclear claims.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_nima_esh","name":"Nima Esh","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","description":"Nima tends a family plot in the Mangrove Terraces and maintains the silt-traps that protect its rice beds. She is a middle-aged, broad-faced woman with a silver streak in her braid and stained reed gloves tucked into her belt. After her parents lived through the Great Silting, she learned how quickly a clogged lock becomes a hunger, but also how easily arguments over silt can divide neighbors who need one another.","motivation":"Keep the terraces fertile and prevent another season of hunger caused by a failing tide.","goal":"Make sure any silt dredged from the locks reaches the terrace plots in time to benefit the next growing season.","flaw":"She assumes people with formal authority will put their own interests first and sometimes withholds useful knowledge until they prove otherwise.","internal_conflict":"Nima wants the terraces to stand together, yet fears that trusting the guilds or ferry crews will cost her neighbors their share of the silt.","external_conflict":"The wardens, ferry cooperative, and glassblower guild must agree on dredging and its timing, while the terraces depend on both a working tide and the fertile silt.","arc":"Nima begins by guarding her terrace knowledge and expecting the powerful factions to bargain past the growers. When Sena brings the survey to the terraces and Tavi commits a barge to the dredging, Nima chooses to organize growers to prepare the silt-traps and receive the load under the silt-debt rule. She ends as an active broker between the crews and the terraces rather than a wary observer waiting to be overlooked.","personality_traits":["steadfast","practical","protective","slow to trust"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silt-trap tending","description":"Maintains root-garden silt-traps and judges where fertile deposits will best support the terraces.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Grower organizing","description":"Coordinates neighbors around planting, shared labor, and the distribution of terrace resources.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_sena_meren","source_character_id":"chr_sena_var","target_character_id":"chr_meren_kai","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sena Var needs Meren Kai to pause the guild's firing season, while Meren initially doubts her warning and sees her demand as a threat to his guild's livelihood."},{"id":"rel_meren_sena","source_character_id":"chr_meren_kai","target_character_id":"chr_sena_var","relationship_type":"skeptical ally","description":"Meren Kai comes to respect Sena Var's survey after the bell check, but remains protective of the guild's work as they coordinate the pause."},{"id":"rel_sena_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_sena_var","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","relationship_type":"tense ally","description":"Sena Var needs Tavi Ro's barges for dredging; Tavi supports the urgent work but presses Sena to recognize the cooperative's silt claim."},{"id":"rel_tavi_nima","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_ro","target_character_id":"chr_nima_esh","relationship_type":"negotiating partners","description":"Tavi Ro's crews haul the fertile silt that Nima Esh's terraces need, and Nima insists that their agreement fulfill the obligation to spread it within a season."},{"id":"rel_nima_sena","source_character_id":"chr_nima_esh","target_character_id":"chr_sena_var","relationship_type":"cautious ally","description":"Nima Esh helps Sena Var connect the lock emergency to the terraces' needs, while testing whether Sena will include growers in the plan."}]}
