ts that enforcing the covenant also means applying its protections fairly to a disowned bearer.","personality_traits":["precise","patient","guarded","conscientious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Covenant memory","description":"Recalls the procedures for recording challenges and the obligations established by the Crane Banner pact.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Witness's voice","description":"Can hold a contentious gathering to formal order by stating the challenge rules clearly and without favor.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_bannerhall","faction_id":"fac_crane_sect"},{"id":"chr_talan","name":"Talan Vey","role":"supporting","description":"A Salt Warden charged with guaranteeing safe conduct for envoys on Saltmarket Isle, Talan has watched old grievances turn trade meetings into tests of loyalty. He is compact and quick-footed, with salt-white cuffs and a market-worn sash that marks his office rather than a martial school. He has no claim to the rookery, but understands how a dispute over food can close routes and leave every isle poorer.","motivation":"Preserve the market peace that lets rival schools trade without surrendering their claims.","goal":"Get the summoned envoys safely to Saltmarket Isle and persuade them to keep the moot open long enough to hear each side.","flaw":"He avoids taking a clear position for fear that either side will stop trusting his neutrality.","internal_conflict":"He believes neutrality protects people, but worries that staying neutral while the rookery is endangered makes him complicit in the harm.","external_conflict":"The unresolved tally dispute threatens to keep envoys away, while tensions between the Crane Sect and Eel School risk undoing the market peace.","arc":"Talan begins by believing his only useful role is to prevent direct confrontation. When Suyin's safe-conduct depends on him naming the market's obligations aloud, he publicly guarantees her passage and calls for the envoys to hear the tally's terms. By the end, he still refuses to choose a fishing claimant, but no longer confuses neutrality with silence.","personality_traits":["diplomatic","wary","resourceful","fair-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe-conduct negotiation","description":"Uses the Salt Wardens' market-peace customs to arrange safe passage and meetings between rival envoys.","category":"social"},{"name":"Market listening","description":"Learns which concerns are driving a dispute by listening to traders and visitors without promising favors.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_suyin_qiao","source_character_id":"chr_suyin","target_character_id":"chr_qiao","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Suyin needs Qiao Ren to honor the tally and send an envoy; Qiao questions her standing and opposes the nesting ban she carries."},{"id":"rel_qiao_suyin","source_character_id":"chr_qiao","target_character_id":"chr_suyin","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Qiao Ren sees Suyin as the bearer of a tally that could bind his school before its fishing claim is heard, while her challenge forces him to confront the covenant's rules."},{"id":"rel_suyin_meilin","source_character_id":"chr_suyin","target_character_id":"chr_meilin","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mei Lin's ruling on the tally can validate Suyin's mission, but Suyin must trust the covenant-keeper to judge the presentation openly."},{"id":"rel_meilin_qiao","source_character_id":"chr_meilin","target_character_id":"chr_qiao","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mei Lin is responsible for upholding the Crane Sect's covenant, while Qiao Ren argues that its nesting ban unfairly limits the Eel School's ancestral fishing rights."},{"id":"rel_talan_suyin","source_character_id":"chr_talan","target_character_id":"chr_suyin","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Talan Vey guarantees Suyin's safe conduct to the neutral market isle, giving her a chance to gather the envoys without endorsing her claim in advance."}]}
