 records.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Tether work","description":"Experienced at moving safely along gantries and securing awkward hull sections in microgravity.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ives_kade","name":"Ives Kade","role":"supporting","description":"Ives Kade is a veteran union heat-roster steward who survived the Sail Fire as a junior mirror-shed hand. He helped defend the safety charter ever since, and keeps the roster annotated with the real recovery times crews need rather than the optimistic ones management prefers. Compact and broad-shouldered, he has silvered eyebrows, a heat-pitted tool case, and a careful way of standing with his back to shade.","home_location_id":"loc_mirror_shed","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union","motivation":"Protect workers from a return to the dangerous shift practices that preceded the Sail Fire.","goal":"Keep the union's heat-budget records intact and force the owners to honor the logged limits.","flaw":"He confuses caution with protection and can withhold information from the very people he means to shield.","internal_conflict":"He wants younger riggers to challenge unsafe orders, but fears that exposing the union's records will let the consortium dismantle its authority.","external_conflict":"Helio Tank is pressing for longer sunside shifts, while the disputed scrap hull could turn the audit into a seizure of the mass ledger and heat-roster records.","arc":"Ives begins by quietly restricting access to roster details, convinced that secrecy is the best defense against Helio Tank. When Mara's evidence shows that the disputed hull's live feed may have required crews to exceed logged limits, he chooses to hand the relevant roster entries to the auditors and stand beside her account. He ends willing to defend the charter in the open, accepting that protection without workers' informed consent repeats the control he opposes.","personality_traits":["protective","patient","wary","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Heat-roster judgment","description":"Can identify when a proposed sunside shift exceeds a crew's logged heat budget.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew mediation","description":"Can negotiate practical work rotations between exhausted crews and supervisors.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_selin_or","name":"Selin Or","role":"supporting","description":"Selin Or is a charter auditor stationed at the Bastion Hulk, sent to reconcile the yard's mass ledger after earlier fraud led to the permanent audit berth. She learned to distrust explanations that cannot be reconciled with physical inventory, but has seen how a ledger can also be used to punish workers for decisions made above them. She is spare and precise, with close-cropped hair, a graphite-colored audit suit, and a slate secured to her wrist.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_charter_audit","motivation":"Make the mass ledger reliable enough that neither owners nor crews can quietly alter what the yard owns.","goal":"Determine whether the scrapped hull remains in the yard's inventory and establish who authorized its power draw.","flaw":"She overvalues documentary proof and assumes that a clean chain of custody is always available to honest witnesses.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be impartial, yet knows that an audit can become a tool for the owners if she treats missing records as workers' guilt.","external_conflict":"The hull is hidden in Shadow Dock beyond thermal survey, the ledger may omit it, and her audit authority is being used to rush a finding before the evidence can be checked.","arc":"Selin begins determined to treat the ledger as the most dependable account of the yard. When Mara brings power measurements that cannot be matched to any logged hull, Selin chooses to preserve the discrepancy and delay a clean audit finding, despite pressure to close the books. She ends by combining physical inspection, crew testimony, and ledger entries, addressing her reliance on paperwork without abandoning the evidence standards her role requires.","personality_traits":["precise","reserved","fair-minded","skeptical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger reconciliation","description":"Can trace mass entries through salvage, hull records, and yard transfers to find inconsistencies.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Evidence interviewing","description":"Can distinguish firsthand observations from assumptions during a formal audit.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_renn","name":"Tomas Renn","role":"antagonist","description":"Tomas Renn is the Helio Tank Consortium's yard operations director, responsible for keeping the chartered facility productive and its scrap contracts profitable. He came up through procurement rather than rigging and believes a yard that cannot meet its schedule will be replaced by one that can. Tall and impeccably groomed, he wears a cooling collar even in the Bastion Hulk and carries a polished mass-tag punch as if it were a badge of office.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"Preserve Helio Tank's revenue and his standing by keeping the yard's salvage contracts and schedules intact.","goal":"Prevent the auditors from finding an unlogged hull before the consortium can decide how to resolve the discrepancy.","flaw":"He regards people and safety rules as adjustable costs whenever they interfere with a deadline.","internal_conflict":"He sees himself as a practical steward of a fragile enterprise, but suspects that his efficiency measures have made the yard dependent on hidden exceptions.","external_conflict":"Mara's power readings, Ives's heat-roster records, and Selin's audit could expose a hull kept off the mass ledger and intensify the dispute over longer sunside shifts.","arc":"Tomas begins convinced that controlled ambiguity is necessary to keep the yard solvent and assumes the audit can be managed as another schedule problem. When Selin preserves the ledger discrepancy and Mara's crew prepares a verifiable inspection of Shadow Dock, he must choose whether to order a rushed shutdown or allow the evidence to be recorded. He chooses to delay the inspection and protect the consortium's position, but the decision makes his role in the concealment visible; by the end, he can no longer present himself as a neutral operator and must answer for treating safety and accounting rules as optional.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","impatient","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract leverage","description":"Knows how to use salvage terms and schedule commitments to pressure yard departments.","category":"social"},{"name":"Operations planning","description":"Can coordinate berth assignments, work windows, and material flows across the yard.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ives","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ives_kade","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ives Kade taught Mara Voss to read heat rosters and salvage records; his habit of withholding information now frustrates her just as she needs his support."},{"id":"rel_ives_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ives_kade","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"protector","description":"Ives Kade wants to protect Mara Voss from a reckless accusation, but his caution risks leaving her alone against the consortium."},{"id":"rel_mara_selin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_selin_or","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mara Voss needs Selin Or to preserve the power discrepancy in the audit, while Selin requires Mara to separate measured evidence from suspicion."},{"id":"rel_selin_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_selin_or","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_renn","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Selin Or's obligation to reconcile the mass ledger conflicts with Tomas Renn's effort to keep the hull discrepancy from becoming an official finding."},{"id":"rel_