out abandoning the evidence standards her role requires.","personality_traits":["precise","reserved","fair-minded","skeptical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger reconciliation","description":"Can trace mass entries through salvage, hull records, and yard transfers to find inconsistencies.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Evidence interviewing","description":"Can distinguish firsthand observations from assumptions during a formal audit.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_renn","name":"Tomas Renn","role":"antagonist","description":"Tomas Renn is the Helio Tank Consortium's yard operations director, responsible for keeping the chartered facility productive and its scrap contracts profitable. He came up through procurement rather than rigging and believes a yard that cannot meet its schedule will be replaced by one that can. Tall and impeccably groomed, he wears a cooling collar even in the Bastion Hulk and carries a polished mass-tag punch as if it were a badge of office.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"Preserve Helio Tank's revenue and his standing by keeping the yard's salvage contracts and schedules intact.","goal":"Prevent the auditors from finding an unlogged hull before the consortium can decide how to resolve the discrepancy.","flaw":"He regards people and safety rules as adjustable costs whenever they interfere with a deadline.","internal_conflict":"He sees himself as a practical steward of a fragile enterprise, but suspects that his efficiency measures have made the yard dependent on hidden exceptions.","external_conflict":"Mara's power readings, Ives's heat-roster records, and Selin's audit could expose a hull kept off the mass ledger and intensify the dispute over longer sunside shifts.","arc":"Tomas begins convinced that controlled ambiguity is necessary to keep the yard solvent and assumes the audit can be managed as another schedule problem. When Selin preserves the ledger discrepancy and Mara's crew prepares a verifiable inspection of Shadow Dock, he must choose whether to order a rushed shutdown or allow the evidence to be recorded. He chooses to delay the inspection and protect the consortium's position, but the decision makes his role in the concealment visible; by the end, he can no longer present himself as a neutral operator and must answer for treating safety and accounting rules as optional.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","impatient","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract leverage","description":"Knows how to use salvage terms and schedule commitments to pressure yard departments.","category":"social"},{"name":"Operations planning","description":"Can coordinate berth assignments, work windows, and material flows across the yard.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ives","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ives_kade","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ives Kade taught Mara Voss to read heat rosters and salvage records; his habit of withholding information now frustrates her just as she needs his support."},{"id":"rel_ives_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ives_kade","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"protector","description":"Ives Kade wants to protect Mara Voss from a reckless accusation, but his caution risks leaving her alone against the consortium."},{"id":"rel_mara_selin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_selin_or","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mara Voss needs Selin Or to preserve the power discrepancy in the audit, while Selin requires Mara to separate measured evidence from suspicion."},{"id":"rel_selin_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_selin_or","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_renn","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Selin Or's obligation to reconcile the mass ledger conflicts with Tomas Renn's effort to keep the hull discrepancy from becoming an official finding."},{"id":"rel_tomas_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_renn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tomas Renn sees Mara Voss's investigation as a threat to the yard's schedule and contracts; Mara sees his pressure as evidence that the records need scrutiny."}]}
