{"world_id":"wld_seedways","characters":[{"id":"chr_nara_vell","name":"Nara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A Seed Keeper raised among the terraced vaults of Granary Hill, Nara learned to grade kernels by hand before she was trusted to carry sealed stock between the valleys. She is lean and weather-browned, with a close-cropped braid threaded through a brass seed-counting ring. After the Millers' Split, she inherited her mother's belief that a keeper's records must be beyond question; she now leads a caravan carrying grain toward the recovering towns and the Frost Gate.","motivation":"Keep the seed stock viable and the caravan's oath intact without letting another generation inherit the old route feud.","goal":"Reach the three recovering valley towns before the last frost, settle the disputed tithe, and restore a shared route through Ford Market.","flaw":"She treats careful procedure as a substitute for listening, especially when someone questions a keeper's ledger.","internal_conflict":"She fears that admitting uncertainty will make the Seed Keepers seem unworthy of trust, even when silence is doing greater harm.","external_conflict":"The diluted tithe at Ford Market has turned millers and keepers against each other, while orchard families dispute what stock the caravan is carrying and the Frost Gate's closing leaves little time.","arc":"Nara begins convinced that a perfectly kept tally can settle any grievance. When the orchard families show her that the sealed allotment excludes promised grafting stock, she chooses to open the caravan's own measures for a public count rather than defend the ledger on authority alone. By the end, she still guards the seed carefully but accepts shared accounting and testimony as part of keeping faith.","home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers","personality_traits":["meticulous","patient","guarded","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seed grading","description":"Sorts viable seed from damaged grain by sight, touch, and smell, and can recognize when a measure has been diluted with chaff.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Caravan planning","description":"Rations stock and estimates hand-and-beast travel time well enough to judge whether the caravan can reach the pass before it closes.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tovin_ree","name":"Tovin Ree","role":"antagonist","description":"A Ford Market miller and keeper of the weigh-house ledgers, Tovin grew up hearing that the Millers' Compact had been blamed for the old split whether or not its books were honest. He is broad-shouldered, with flour caught in the seams of his dark coat and a thumb stained by ledger ink. He knows the market's measures intimately and has quietly mixed chaff into a portion of the tithe grain, telling himself the diversion will protect local stores from a bad return harvest.","motivation":"Keep Ford Market from surrendering grain it may need to survive the next poor harvest, and avoid seeing the Compact condemned again.","goal":"Prevent the caravan from taking the full disputed measure until the market has secured enough grain for its own people.","flaw":"He makes secret decisions on behalf of others and assumes that a useful lie is safer than an open argument.","internal_conflict":"He wants the Compact to be trusted, but believes honesty will expose its weakness and cost him the influence he uses to protect the market.","external_conflict":"His chaff-diluted tithe has made the Seed Keepers suspect the millers, revived the feud over the forged ledger, and jeopardized the caravan's time at Ford Market.","arc":"Tovin begins by hiding the adulteration and treating suspicion as proof that the market must defend itself. When Nara agrees to a public count and he sees the discrepancy cannot be blamed on the old feud, he chooses to identify the altered measure and enter the shortfall in the ledger under his own name. He ends with less control over the Compact but begins repairing trust through an honest account and a proposed repayment from future harvest measures.","home_location_id":"loc_ford_market","faction_id":"fac_millers_compact","personality_traits":["shrewd","protective","defensive","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market measures","description":"Can check weights and measures by hand and spot inconsistencies in the weigh-house's grain tallies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bargaining","description":"Reads the limits and priorities of market negotiations, though he has often used that skill to delay rather than resolve a dispute.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_esa_morn","name":"Esa Morn","role":"supporting","description":"An Orchard Families planter who took a plot on the blight-ash soil when others still considered it lost ground. Esa has ash-gray curls, a grafting knife worn smooth from years of use, and pale scars across both palms from clearing burned roots. Her family has waited for grafting stock promised by the vaults; she has come to meet the caravan because she suspects its grain will pass through the orchards without leaving what her people are owed.","motivation":"Secure grafting stock for the families who accepted the hardest land and make their claim impossible to dismiss.","goal":"Have the caravan set aside and record the promised stock before it leaves the Ash Orchards.","flaw":"She turns old neglect into a reason to distrust every offer, even when cooperation could strengthen her claim.","internal_conflict":"She wants the orchards to belong to a shared recovery, yet fears that relying on the seedways will once again leave her families last in line.","external_conflict":"The caravan's disputed allotment appears to take grain past the orchards, while the approaching frost threatens to delay both the journey and any grafting stock meant for her families.","arc":"Esa begins ready to block the caravan until it meets her demand, believing any compromise will erase the orchard families' claim. When Nara opens the sealed measures for a shared count, Esa chooses to witness and record the allotment instead of seizing stock from the caravan. She ends with a written claim tied to the tithe account and a place in the route's reckoning, having defended her people without cutting them off from the seedway.","home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families","personality_traits":["resolute","observant","proud","practical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Joins orchard stock by hand and can judge which young grafts are most likely to take in recovering soil.","category":"other"},{"name":"Ash-soil knowledge","description":"Recognizes the signs of blight-ash ground that will support a planting and those that need another season of tending.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_bren_hal","name":"Bren Hal","role":"supporting","description":"A caravan hauler from the high approach to the Frost Gate, Bren has spent years moving sacks by pack beast and shoulder along routes that vanish under snow. He is rangy and stooped from carrying loads, with a patched wool hood and a small wooden tally board hanging at his belt. His family once wintered beyond the closing pass after a route dispute delayed their return; he joined the caravan so no one would mistake a dangerous delay for a harmless one.","motivation":"Keep the caravan moving safely and prevent another party from being stranded beyond the Frost Gate.","goal":"Convince the others to leave Ford Market in time to cross the pass, without abandoning a fair settlement of the grain dispute.","flaw":"He retreats into caution and silence, expecting that speaking up will only make others ignore the danger.","internal_conflict":"He wants to honor the caravan's obligations, but fears that stopping to repair old harms will repeat the loss his family suffered.","external_conflict":"The weigh-house dispute and competing claims consume time while the Frost Gate closes on the last frost, putting the caravan and its stock at risk of being stranded.","arc":"Bren begins by quietly urging an early departure and letting louder voices decide what counts as urgent. When the public count at Ford Market threatens to delay the caravan, he lays out his family's account of being stranded beyond the pass and offers a practical schedule for completing the count before they leave. He ends willing to speak plainly about danger without using it to shut down the claims that the caravan must honor.","home_location_id":"loc_frost_gate","personality_traits":["cautious","reliable","reserved","enduring"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pass judgment","description":"Reads weather, snow signs, and the condition of the high trail to estimate when the Frost Gate will become unsafe.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Load handling","description":"Balances seed sacks on pack beasts and secures them with salvaged hand-made harnesses for rough trails.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nara_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_ree","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nara Vell and Tovin Ree clash over the diluted tithe: Nara demands an honest count, while Tovin hides the shortfall to protect Ford Market."},{"id":"rel_tovin_nara","source_character_id":"chr_tovin_ree","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","relationship_type":"distrust","description":"Tovin Ree distrusts Nara Vell's authority as a Seed Keeper, seeing her defense of the sealed tally as a threat to Ford Market."},{"id":"rel_nara_esa","source_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_esa_morn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Nara Vell and Esa Morn share an interest in a transparent allotment, though Esa insists Nara account for the grafting stock owed to the orchards."},{"id":"rel_esa_nara","source_character_id":"chr_esa_morn","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","relationship_type":"distrust","description":"Esa Morn doubts Nara Vell will honor the Orchard Families' claim unless the caravan's measures are opened and recorded."},{"id":"rel_bren_nara","source_character_id":"chr_bren_hal","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Bren Hal supports Nara Vell's attempt to settle the count, but presses her to account for the time remaining before the Frost Gate closes."},{"id":"rel_bren_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_bren_hal","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_ree","relationship_type":"conflicted","description":"Bren Hal resents Tovin Ree's delay at Ford Market because his family was once stranded beyond the Frost Gate after a route dispute."}]}
