or a shared count, Esa chooses to witness and record the allotment instead of seizing stock from the caravan. She ends with a written claim tied to the tithe account and a place in the route's reckoning, having defended her people without cutting them off from the seedway.","home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families","personality_traits":["resolute","observant","proud","practical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Joins orchard stock by hand and can judge which young grafts are most likely to take in recovering soil.","category":"other"},{"name":"Ash-soil knowledge","description":"Recognizes the signs of blight-ash ground that will support a planting and those that need another season of tending.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_bren_hal","name":"Bren Hal","role":"supporting","description":"A caravan hauler from the high approach to the Frost Gate, Bren has spent years moving sacks by pack beast and shoulder along routes that vanish under snow. He is rangy and stooped from carrying loads, with a patched wool hood and a small wooden tally board hanging at his belt. His family once wintered beyond the closing pass after a route dispute delayed their return; he joined the caravan so no one would mistake a dangerous delay for a harmless one.","motivation":"Keep the caravan moving safely and prevent another party from being stranded beyond the Frost Gate.","goal":"Convince the others to leave Ford Market in time to cross the pass, without abandoning a fair settlement of the grain dispute.","flaw":"He retreats into caution and silence, expecting that speaking up will only make others ignore the danger.","internal_conflict":"He wants to honor the caravan's obligations, but fears that stopping to repair old harms will repeat the loss his family suffered.","external_conflict":"The weigh-house dispute and competing claims consume time while the Frost Gate closes on the last frost, putting the caravan and its stock at risk of being stranded.","arc":"Bren begins by quietly urging an early departure and letting louder voices decide what counts as urgent. When the public count at Ford Market threatens to delay the caravan, he lays out his family's account of being stranded beyond the pass and offers a practical schedule for completing the count before they leave. He ends willing to speak plainly about danger without using it to shut down the claims that the caravan must honor.","home_location_id":"loc_frost_gate","personality_traits":["cautious","reliable","reserved","enduring"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pass judgment","description":"Reads weather, snow signs, and the condition of the high trail to estimate when the Frost Gate will become unsafe.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Load handling","description":"Balances seed sacks on pack beasts and secures them with salvaged hand-made harnesses for rough trails.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nara_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_ree","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nara Vell and Tovin Ree clash over the diluted tithe: Nara demands an honest count, while Tovin hides the shortfall to protect Ford Market."},{"id":"rel_tovin_nara","source_character_id":"chr_tovin_ree","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","relationship_type":"distrust","description":"Tovin Ree distrusts Nara Vell's authority as a Seed Keeper, seeing her defense of the sealed tally as a threat to Ford Market."},{"id":"rel_nara_esa","source_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_esa_morn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Nara Vell and Esa Morn share an interest in a transparent allotment, though Esa insists Nara account for the grafting stock owed to the orchards."},{"id":"rel_esa_nara","source_character_id":"chr_esa_morn","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","relationship_type":"distrust","description":"Esa Morn doubts Nara Vell will honor the Orchard Families' claim unless the caravan's measures are opened and recorded."},{"id":"rel_bren_nara","source_character_id":"chr_bren_hal","target_character_id":"chr_nara_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Bren Hal supports Nara Vell's attempt to settle the count, but presses her to account for the time remaining before the Frost Gate closes."},{"id":"rel_bren_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_bren_hal","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_ree","relationship_type":"conflicted","description":"Bren Hal resents Tovin Ree's delay at Ford Market because his family was once stranded beyond the Frost Gate after a route dispute."}]}
