[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_underworld_ledger","characters":[{"id":"chr_ira_quill","name":"Ira Quill","role":"protagonist","description":"A junior clerk of the Order of Scribes, Ira learned to keep her head down among the crowded desks of the Counting Halls. She is slight, ink-stained, and meticulous enough to notice that a mortal life has been entered under the wrong ledger column. Her first instinct is to trust the procedure that trained her; the miscast tally forces her to carry its correction through offices that would rather blame one another.","motivation":"To prove that careful work can still protect the dead in a system that treats mistakes as someone else's fault.","goal":"Secure the three seals needed to correct the ledger before the soul is weighed.","flaw":"She mistakes precision and obedience for courage, delaying action until she can make every risk look procedural.","internal_conflict":"Ira fears that challenging a signed entry will expose her own earlier habit of copying without questioning.","external_conflict":"The Order of Scribes and the Collegium of Weighers blame one another for rising miscast tallies, while the soul's weighing approaches and a miscast account could send it to the Erasure Wells.","arc":"Ira begins as a gifted copyist who believes a flawless form is safer than a difficult truth. When the Weigher's warrant stalls her request to inspect the sealed ledger, she chooses to carry the correction onward and put her own copying record under scrutiny. She ends willing to take responsibility for an imperfect process rather than let procedure disguise a preventable wrong.","home_location_id":"loc_counting_halls","faction_id":"fac_scribes_order","personality_traits":["observant","dry-witted","cautious","persistent"],"abilities":[{"name":"Column memory","description":"Can recall the layout and wording of ledger entries she has carefully transcribed.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Clerk's hand","description":"Copies dense accounts legibly and quickly, making discrepancies easier to compare.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_vesper_dane","name":"Vesper Dane","role":"supporting","description":"Newly arrived at the Gate of Receipts, Vesper is a mortal soul whose tally-slip bears the wrong column mark. In life, Vesper kept a small account book of promises made and debts repaid, a habit that left them skeptical of anyone who claims a ledger is neutral. Their gray travel coat still holds the creases of a long journey, though they now wait in the queue with no prospect of returning to the living.","motivation":"To have the account judged by what was actually written about their life, not by a clerical error.","goal":"Make the officials compare the tally-slip with the original record before the weighing.","flaw":"Vesper treats every offer of help as a bargain with hidden terms.","internal_conflict":"They want to trust Ira's effort but fear that hope will make the impending judgment harder to face.","external_conflict":"Their soul is queued for weighing against a miscast ledger, and the world offers no appeal after an account is wrongly balanced into the Erasure Wells.","arc":"Vesper begins guarded, insisting that no clerk deserves their trust. When Ira risks her standing to carry the correction, Vesper chooses to give her the tally-slip and recount the details needed to identify the error. They end still wary, but willing to place their account in another person's hands without mistaking that trust for a promise of rescue.","home_location_id":"loc_gate_of_receipts","personality_traits":["skeptical","wry","self-possessed","attentive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tally-slip recall","description":"Remembers the marks and wording on the receipt surrendered at arrival, including the disputed column.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tovan_reed","name":"Tovan Reed","role":"supporting","description":"A certification officer of the Collegium of Weighers, Tovan has spent years ensuring that each soul is measured against a properly attested account. Broad-shouldered and impeccably dressed, he carries himself like a balance that must never tip. His caution comes from the War of the Wrong Column, whose double-weighings taught the courts how quickly one office's certainty can become another office's catastrophe.","motivation":"To prevent an uncertified correction from reviving the old abuses of rival weigher houses.","goal":"Require a valid warrant and the full three-key seal before any ledger is changed.","flaw":"He uses precedent to avoid admitting when a rule is protecting his office more than the dead.","internal_conflict":"Tovan believes restraint prevents injustice, yet knows that refusing to act on a clear error can itself become an injustice.","external_conflict":"The Sealed Ledgers dispute bars archive access without a weigher's warrant, while the approaching weighing makes delay dangerous and the scribes accuse his office of causing the miscast tallies.","arc":"Tovan begins convinced that refusing an incomplete petition is the only safe course. When Ira presents Vesper's receipt and accepts scrutiny of her own transcription, he must choose between shielding his office and issuing the warrant that allows the sealed record to be checked. He ends prepared to certify a correction supported by evidence, not merely one that protects the Collegium from blame.","home_location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","faction_id":"fac_weighers","personality_traits":["formal","measured","proud","uneasy"],"abilities":[{"name":"Balance reading","description":"Can identify when a soul's measured account does not match the certified figures presented for weighing.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Procedural authority","description":"Can issue a weigher's warrant for review of a sealed ledger when the evidence meets his office's standards.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_wick","name":"Sella Wick","role":"supporting","description":"A keeper of the Lamp Archive, Sella tends the sealed stacks by lamplight and knows how easily an old entry can vanish behind layers of dust and procedure. She is spare, silver-haired, and careful never to read a sealed page aloud: the Lamp Seal's oath would cost her lamp and post. Her silence has kept the archive intact, but it has also made her a convenient guardian of records no one else can inspect.","motivation":"To preserve the archive without letting its rules become a cover for errors.","goal":"Help verify the disputed account while keeping the sealed page from being read aloud.","flaw":"She hides behind silence even when there are lawful ways to help.","internal_conflict":"Sella fears that speaking against the archive's habits will cost her the post that gives her purpose, but fears more that silence will make her stewardship meaningless.","external_conflict":"The Lamplighter Kin refuse to open sealed ledgers without a weigher's warrant, and the oath forbids Sella from reading a sealed page aloud.","arc":"Sella begins treating silence as the only way to honor her lamp oath. When Tovan's warrant reaches the archive, she chooses to open the relevant ledger for inspection and point Ira to the written entry without reading it aloud. She ends having risked institutional displeasure while keeping her oath, understanding that restraint need not mean refusal.","home_location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","faction_id":"fac_lamplighters","personality_traits":["patient","guarded","wry","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Archive keeping","description":"Can locate old ledger entries by their seals, dates, and filing marks without voicing their contents.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Lamp tending","description":"Keeps the archive's lamps steady enough to inspect faded pages and worn seals.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ira_vesper","source_character_id":"chr_ira_quill","target_character_id":"chr_vesper_dane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ira works to correct Vesper's account before the weighing; Vesper's mistrust challenges Ira to earn confidence through actions rather than paperwork."},{"id":"rel_ira_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_ira_quill","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_reed","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ira needs Tovan's warrant to reach the sealed ledger, while Tovan's procedural caution frustrates her urgent attempt to prevent Vesper's miscast weighing."},{"id":"rel_sella_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_sella_wick","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_reed","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sella and Tovan must cooperate to inspect the sealed record; each distrusts the other's office's role in the rising miscast tallies."},{"id":"rel_vesper_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_vesper_dane","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_reed","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Vesper sees Tovan's insistence on warrants as another obstacle between a soul and a fair weighing, while Tovan must decide whether to treat Vesper's claim as evidence or merely a plea."}]}
</Output>
