s not belong in the established pattern.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Foundry craft","description":"Uses hand tools and practical knowledge of bronze to inspect casting marks and surface flaws.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_aldren_marr","name":"Aldren Marr","role":"supporting","description":"A senior founder of the Founder Collegium, Aldren has spent decades answering for the bells and carrying the weight of the maker’s mark on each one. His left ear is scarred from years near the furnaces, and he wears a soot-stained coat with a small brass gauge tucked into its pocket. He taught Nera to listen before touching a bell, but his reputation rests on the claim that every ring can be traced to a known caster. The unmarked sound threatens not only his standing but the certainty on which he has built his life.","home_location_id":"loc_founder_row","faction_id":"fac_bell_founders","motivation":"Preserve the Founder Collegium’s credibility and keep the bells ringing.","goal":"Find a defensible explanation for the strange pattern before the Watch imposes silence.","flaw":"He treats public certainty as more important than private truth.","internal_conflict":"Aldren wants to protect the craft he devoted his life to, but fears that acknowledging what he cannot explain will make the founders appear fraudulent.","external_conflict":"The Watch demands the bells be stilled, while Nera's evidence challenges his insistence that every note must have a known maker.","arc":"Aldren begins by dismissing Nera’s concern and insisting that the Collegium can account for every bell. When the pattern returns at the Sea-Wall Belfry despite his inspection, he must choose between backing the Watch’s silence order or publicly admitting that the founders cannot explain the sound. He shares the Collegium’s records with Nera and the wardens, ending less certain of his own authority but more willing to defend the city through candor.","personality_traits":["disciplined","proud","protective","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Casting records","description":"Can read makers’ marks and compare them with the Founder Collegium’s records of the bells.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bell inspection","description":"Recognizes common bronze flaws and tuning problems through careful examination and listening.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_rook","name":"Tamsin Rook","role":"antagonist","description":"A senior warden of the Parish Watch, Tamsin reads writs at Bailiff’s Stairs and enforces the silence laws with a reputation for unyielding order. She is spare-built, close-cropped, and immaculate in a dark watch coat that always smells faintly of lamp oil. After seeing how quickly a spoken name can vanish into fog, she came to believe that strict control is the only protection the city can trust. The Watch’s power to still a bell by writ gives her a practical answer to the crisis, even if that answer may leave the wall undefended.","home_location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","faction_id":"fac_parish_watch","motivation":"Keep citizens alive and preserve the silence laws that guard them from the Chiming.","goal":"Enforce the order to silence the storm-bells before the next fog can take hold.","flaw":"She mistakes obedience for safety and acts before hearing evidence that complicates her orders.","internal_conflict":"Tamsin fears that allowing an unexplained ring to continue will invite catastrophe, but suspects that silencing the bells may expose the city to the very danger she is trying to prevent.","external_conflict":"Nera and Aldren challenge the Watch’s writ with evidence that the strange pattern may be part of the threat, while the fog draws near.","arc":"Tamsin begins determined to silence the bells as soon as the writ permits, treating discussion as an unacceptable risk. When the pattern sounds again at the Sea-Wall Belfry and Nera presents the Collegium’s evidence, Tamsin must choose whether to enforce the writ blindly or delay it long enough to test what the ring means. She grants that brief hearing and helps keep the bells under watch, ending still cautious but no longer equating control with protection.","personality_traits":["decisive","stern","vigilant","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Writ enforcement","description":"Can organize wardens and carry out parish orders, including the lawful stilling of a bell.","category":"social"},{"name":"Fog discipline","description":"Uses name-tokens and signs to coordinate with others without speaking names in fog.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_vesper_quill","name":"Vesper Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A licensed Fog Broker who keeps a narrow stall in the Fogmarket, Vesper trades in names and secrets under the Brokers’ Charter. Their elegant gloves conceal ink-stained fingers, and a brass-framed mask rests at their throat for nights when the fog makes speech perilous. Vesper remembers the names attached to debts better than the faces that incurred them, a skill that has made them useful and deeply distrusted. They have learned to survive by never giving information without expecting something in return.","home_location_id":"loc_fogmarket","faction_id":"fac_fog_brokers","motivation":"Keep the Fog Brokers’ charter intact and prevent the Watch from using the crisis to seize the market’s trade.","goal":"Uncover what the strange bell pattern is connected to before the Watch shuts down the Fogmarket.","flaw":"They turn every relationship into a transaction, even when cooperation would serve them better.","internal_conflict":"Vesper depends on secrecy to stay safe, yet their knowledge of name-debts could help resolve a crisis threatening the whole city.","external_conflict":"The Watch calls the brokers’ name-debts extortion and may close their market, while the bells’ strange pattern stirs fear among their customers.","arc":"Vesper begins by offering Nera only a bargain for information about the bell pattern, unwilling to risk anything without payment.