","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Casting records","description":"Can read makers’ marks and compare them with the Founder Collegium’s records of the bells.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bell inspection","description":"Recognizes common bronze flaws and tuning problems through careful examination and listening.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_rook","name":"Tamsin Rook","role":"antagonist","description":"A senior warden of the Parish Watch, Tamsin reads writs at Bailiff’s Stairs and enforces the silence laws with a reputation for unyielding order. She is spare-built, close-cropped, and immaculate in a dark watch coat that always smells faintly of lamp oil. After seeing how quickly a spoken name can vanish into fog, she came to believe that strict control is the only protection the city can trust. The Watch’s power to still a bell by writ gives her a practical answer to the crisis, even if that answer may leave the wall undefended.","home_location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","faction_id":"fac_parish_watch","motivation":"Keep citizens alive and preserve the silence laws that guard them from the Chiming.","goal":"Enforce the order to silence the storm-bells before the next fog can take hold.","flaw":"She mistakes obedience for safety and acts before hearing evidence that complicates her orders.","internal_conflict":"Tamsin fears that allowing an unexplained ring to continue will invite catastrophe, but suspects that silencing the bells may expose the city to the very danger she is trying to prevent.","external_conflict":"Nera and Aldren challenge the Watch’s writ with evidence that the strange pattern may be part of the threat, while the fog draws near.","arc":"Tamsin begins determined to silence the bells as soon as the writ permits, treating discussion as an unacceptable risk. When the pattern sounds again at the Sea-Wall Belfry and Nera presents the Collegium’s evidence, Tamsin must choose whether to enforce the writ blindly or delay it long enough 