[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_comet_market","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A guild factotum of the Mapmakers' Guild, Mara grew up carrying sealed claims between the Map House and the Long Hall, learning every clause of the burn articles but rarely being trusted to decide a case. Now appointed arbiter of the stolen star-map dispute, she is lean and quick-footed, with a close-cropped braid, ink-stained cuffs, and a brass tally ring she turns whenever a hearing grows tense.","home_location_id":"loc_long_hall","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","motivation":"Prove that fair arbitration can protect the fleet better than guild privilege or a strong claimant's purse.","goal":"Determine who has the right to the sealed perihelion map and settle the claim before the comet reaches its burn.","flaw":"She hides behind procedure when a decision might make her personally responsible for someone's loss.","internal_conflict":"Mara believes impartiality means keeping her own judgment out of the case, even when strict procedure favors those who already hold power.","external_conflict":"The Mapmakers' Guild expects her to condemn the pilot holding the map, while the pilot calls it salvage and the ice barons are buying tether rights ahead of the burn.","arc":"Mara begins as a meticulous factotum who treats rules as shelter from blame. When the hearing reveals that the map's resale would leave indebted pilots without a safe route or tether, she chooses to open it under her authority as arbiter and enter the route evidence into the Long Hall record, despite guild pressure. She ends willing to make a defensible judgment openly and accept its consequences rather than let procedure conceal an unjust outcome.","personality_traits":["observant","methodical","dry-witted","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Burn-article expertise","description":"Can interpret claims, tether obligations, and arbitration procedure under the market's burn articles.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Claim mediation","description":"Can draw hostile parties into a formal hearing and identify what each is actually willing to concede.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_kest","name":"Ren Kest","role":"supporting","description":"A Free Pilots' Compact navigator, Ren took possession of the stolen sealed chart after buying it from a desperate intermediary and insists the sale was salvage, not piracy. Years of flying routes the guild only charts have made Ren wary of official maps and official promises. Ren wears a patched pressure coat, keeps a route cord knotted around one wrist, and carries a harpoon line cutter as a practical tool rather than a weapon.","home_location_id":"loc_tether_docks","faction_id":"fac_free_pilots","motivation":"Keep independent pilots from being stranded or forced to fly blind at perihelion.","goal":"Secure recognition of the map as legitimate salvage and use its route information to protect pilot berths through the burn.","flaw":"Ren's suspicion of guild authority turns every negotiation into a test of whether the other side will betray them.","internal_conflict":"Ren wants the Compact to share responsibility for the fleet's safety but fears that surrendering control of the map will restore the guild's monopoly over routes.","external_conflict":"The Mapmakers' Guild calls Ren a pirate and can demand the map be opened at the Long Hall; meanwhile the Ice Barons are buying tethers from pilots who cannot pay their ice-tithes.","arc":"Ren begins determined to keep the map beyond guild reach, trusting only the route knowledge pilots can verify themselves. When Mara offers to enter the opened map into the Long Hall record rather than return it to private guild control, Ren chooses to testify about the salvage sale and the dangers of the route. Ren ends still challenging guild authority, but willing to share evidence and risk a formal judgment to keep other pilots from being stranded.","personality_traits":["resourceful","guarded","bold","loyal to the Compact"],"abilities":[{"name":"Sail and tether handling","description":"Can rig a berth and maneuver a ship using sails, tethers, and reaction plumes.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Route reading","description":"Can assess practical flight risks from a chart and a pilot's knowledge of the comet's orbit.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ivo_senn","name":"Ivo Senn","role":"supporting","description":"The Mapmakers' Guild sealer who authenticated the perihelion chart, Ivo considers a seal a promise that no single claimant may rewrite a route for private gain. Ivo trained under the guild after the Map Wars and still remembers how rival charts nearly wrecked the fleet. Careful and spare in manner, Ivo wears a dark mapmaker's coat with a cracked wax-seal clasp and has a faint scar across one thumb from years of working paper, wax, and cold tools.","home_location_id":"loc_map_house","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","motivation":"Keep the guild's charting system credible enough that pilots can trust a registered route.","goal":"Establish how the sealed map left the Map House and ensure its route is verified before perihelion.","flaw":"Ivo confuses protecting the guild's reputation with protecting the purpose the guild was founded to serve.","internal_conflict":"Ivo knows the guild's monopoly was won after a disaster, yet fears that admitting its failures will invite a return to reckless rival charts.","external_conflict":"The stolen map has been resold to Ren, and the map-seal rule allows only Ivo as sealer or Mara as Long Hall arbiter to open it.","arc":"Ivo begins intent on recovering the map quietly so the guild's authority will not be questioned. When Mara's hearing exposes that the original registry omitted a route hazard Ivo had reported but the guild suppressed, Ivo chooses to confirm the omission and witness the map's opening. Ivo ends committed to restoring trust through accurate records, even when the truth damages the guild's standing.","personality_traits":["precise","reserved","conscientious","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Map sealing","description":"Can authenticate registered star-maps and identify tampering with their seals.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Chart verification","description":"Can compare route records and recognize inconsistencies in a registered map.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sela_vorn","name":"Sela Vorn","role":"antagonist","description":"An Ice Baron claim-holder who has spent several orbits acquiring core claims and buying tether rights before perihelion, Sela sees the burn as the market's clearest test of who planned well and who did not. Sela speaks softly in the Core Vaults and dresses in layered pale workcloth marked with the baron's claim seals, presenting every hard bargain as simple accounting.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","motivation":"Preserve the barons' influence over the market by turning scarce ice and tether rights into dependable leverage.","goal":"Acquire enough indebted pilots' tether rights before the burn to control which ships can remain berthed and which must depart.","flaw":"Sela treats every human obligation as a negotiable claim and mistakes control for security.","internal_conflict":"Sela wants the market to survive perihelion but believes only concentrated ownership can prevent the fleet from dissolving into competing interests.","external_conflict":"Ren's possession of the perihelion map and Mara's arbitration could expose how Sela's tether purchases exploit pilots' unpaid ice-tithes and imperil the fleet.","arc":"Sela begins convinced that buying tether rights is a legitimate way to prepare for the burn. When Mara's ruling links the map's route evidence to the pilots Sela has been pressuring, Sela must choose whether to claim those rights immediately or release enough berths for the fleet to maneuver together. Sela releases a portion to prevent the fleet from scattering, but ends still convinced that concentrated ownership is necessary, now aware that control without the pilots' cooperation cannot secure the market.","personality_traits":["patient","calculating","composed","possessive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claim negotiation","description":"Can structure bargains around ice claims and berth obligations to secure leverage.","category":"social"},{"name":"Resource accounting","description":"Can track ice stores, claim balances, and tether holdings across the market.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_ren_kest","relationship_type":"adversarial allies","description":"Mara Vell must judge Ren Kest's claim to the sealed map, while Ren suspects Mara will favor the Mapmakers' Guild; their uneasy cooperation forces both to risk trusting the hearing."},{"id":"rel_ren_ivo","source_character_id":"chr_ren_kest","target_character_id":"chr_ivo_senn","relationship_type":"rivals","description":"Ren Kest sees Ivo Senn's seal as the guild's grip on routes, while Ivo sees Ren's salvage claim as a threat to the chart registry."},{"id":"rel_sela_ren","source_character_id":"chr_sela_vorn","target_character_id":"chr_ren_kest","relationship_type":"opponents","description":"Sela Vorn's tether purchases threaten the independent pilots Ren Kest represents, and Ren's testimony could expose the costs of Sela's pre-burn strategy."},{"id":"rel_ivo_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ivo_senn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"colleagues","description":"Ivo Senn authenticated the chart Mara Vell must arbitrate; their shared guild background binds them, but Ivo's withheld registry evidence tests Mara's impartiality."},{"id":"rel_sela_mara","source_character_id":"chr_sela_vorn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"adversaries","description":"Sela Vorn wants the burn-arbitration to leave the barons' tether acquisitions intact, while Mara Vell's ruling could limit Sela's leverage over indebted pilots."}]}
</Output>
