ding.","personality_traits":["precise","reserved","conscientious","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Map sealing","description":"Can authenticate registered star-maps and identify tampering with their seals.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Chart verification","description":"Can compare route records and recognize inconsistencies in a registered map.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sela_vorn","name":"Sela Vorn","role":"antagonist","description":"An Ice Baron claim-holder who has spent several orbits acquiring core claims and buying tether rights before perihelion, Sela sees the burn as the market's clearest test of who planned well and who did not. Sela speaks softly in the Core Vaults and dresses in layered pale workcloth marked with the baron's claim seals, presenting every hard bargain as simple accounting.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","motivation":"Preserve the barons' influence over the market by turning scarce ice and tether rights into dependable leverage.","goal":"Acquire enough indebted pilots' tether rights before the burn to control which ships can remain berthed and which must depart.","flaw":"Sela treats every human obligation as a negotiable claim and mistakes control for security.","internal_conflict":"Sela wants the market to survive perihelion but believes only concentrated ownership can prevent the fleet from dissolving into competing interests.","external_conflict":"Ren's possession of the perihelion map and Mara's arbitration could expose how Sela's tether purchases exploit pilots' unpaid ice-tithes and imperil the fleet.","arc":"Sela begins convinced that buying tether rights is a legitimate way to prepare for the burn. When Mara's ruling links the map's route evidence to the pilots Sela has been pressuring, Sela must choose whether to claim those rights immediately or release enough berths for the fleet to maneuver together. Sela releases a portion to prevent the fleet from scattering, but ends still convinced that concentrated ownership is necessary, now aware that control without the pilots' cooperation cannot secure the market.","personality_traits":["patient","calculating","composed","possessive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claim negotiation","description":"Can structure bargains around ice claims and berth obligations to secure leverage.","category":"social"},{"name":"Resource accounting","description":"Can track ice stores, claim balances, and tether holdings across the market.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_ren_kest","relationship_type":"adversarial allies","description":"Mara Vell must judge Ren Kest's claim to the sealed map, while Ren suspects Mara will favor the Mapmakers' Guild; their uneasy cooperation forces both to risk trusting the hearing."},{"id":"rel_ren_ivo","source_character_id":"chr_ren_kest","target_character_id":"chr_ivo_senn","relationship_type":"rivals","description":"Ren Kest sees Ivo Senn's seal as the guild's grip on routes, while Ivo sees Ren's salvage claim as a threat to the chart registry."},{"id":"rel_sela_ren","source_character_id":"chr_sela_vorn","target_character_id":"chr_ren_kest","relationship_type":"opponents","description":"Sela Vorn's tether purchases threaten the independent pilots Ren Kest represents, and Ren's testimony could expose the costs of Sela's pre-burn strategy."},{"id":"rel_ivo_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ivo_senn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"colleagues","description":"Ivo Senn authenticated the chart Mara Vell must arbitrate; their shared guild background binds them, but Ivo's withheld registry evidence tests Mara's impartiality."},{"id":"rel_sela_mara","source_character_id":"chr_sela_vorn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"adversaries","description":"Sela Vorn wants the burn-arbitration to leave the barons' tether acquisitions intact, while Mara Vell's ruling could limit Sela's leverage over indebted pilots."}]}
