{"id":"chr_karim_pilot","name":"Karim","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","description":"Karim is a master pilot who has spent his working life reading the water and wind from the harbour steps. He was a young apprentice when the Ghat Oath became public rite after a pilot was bought to misread the sea, and he has never forgotten how quickly a private suspicion can endanger a whole fleet. Lean and weather-darkened, he wears a faded cotton wrap and keeps a small piece of polished wood for marking wind shifts. He speaks sparingly, preferring a witnessed declaration to a confident prediction.","motivation":"Keep the pilots' declaration worthy of the public trust bound to the Ghat Oath.","goal":"Declare the monsoon turned only when the sea gives clear signs, without letting the court's dispute make him delay or rush the rite.","flaw":"He hides behind procedure when a difficult judgment requires him to explain what he sees.","internal_conflict":"Karim believes the public rite protects the harbour, but worries that the court may use its form to disguise pressure on the pilots.","external_conflict":"The rival claims and the approaching wind turn make every hour consequential, while the Ghat Oath requires a public declaration that cannot be privately purchased.","arc":"Karim begins relying on the rite's formal steps to avoid being drawn into the court's conflict. When the wind shows a clear change as the envoys remain deadlocked, he declares what he observes before the assembled witnesses and explains the signs rather than letting silence serve as cover. He ends treating the Ghat Oath not only as protection from bribery but as a responsibility to speak plainly.","personality_traits":["watchful","disciplined","quiet","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind reading","description":"Reads local sea and wind signs to judge when the monsoon has turned, as required before any fleet may sail.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mira_yusuf","source_character_id":"chr_mira_das","target_character_id":"chr_yusuf_albahr","relationship_type":"cautious ally","description":"Mira Das respects Yusuf al-Bahr's willingness to negotiate, but suspects his patience can conceal a claim he will not readily yield."},{"id":"rel_leon_mira","source_character_id":"chr_leon_varela","target_character_id":"chr_mira_das","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Leon Varela needs Mira Das to certify the filing order, while she refuses to let his certainty substitute for evidence."},{"id":"rel_samira_leon","source_character_id":"chr_samira_bint_rashid","target_character_id":"chr_leon_varela","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Samira bint Rashid and Leon Varela compete for the first slot and distrust each other's accounts of the disputed filing hour."},{"id":"rel_yusuf_samira","source_character_id":"chr_yusuf_albahr","target_character_id":"chr_samira_bint_rashid","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Yusuf al-Bahr wants a settlement Samira bint Rashid can accept, but their delegations' claims cannot both hold the first place."},{"id":"rel_karim_mira","source_character_id":"chr_karim_pilot","target_character_id":"chr_mira_das","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Karim gives Mira Das a public account of the wind's signs, supporting her effort to keep the court's decision separate from pressure on the pilots."},{"id":"rel_samira_mira","source_character_id":"chr_samira_bint_rashid","target_character_id":"chr_mira_das","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Samira bint Rashid wants Mira Das to investigate the ledger, but worries that the scribe's inquiry will expose her delegation's own favors."}]}
