ssure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wick tending","description":"Can trim, set, and relight wall lantern wicks quickly in wind and damp.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Careful observation","description":"Notices small differences in flame, oil level, and soot that others overlook.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_edda_marr","name":"Edda Marr","role":"supporting","description":"A senior Lamp Warden who has spent most of her life at the wall and in the Keeper's Croft, Edda trained generations of wardens to keep the lamps burning without asking what the light might reveal. Her hands are scarred from hot metal and split wick, and her gray hair is bound beneath a soot-dark kerchief. She speaks in measured instructions and keeps old tools arranged in exact order. Edda knows more about the missing ledger page than she admits, having learned that a frightened parish will accept silence more readily than uncertainty.","home_location_id":"loc_lantern_wall","faction_id":"fac_lamp_wardens","motivation":"Keep the wall burning and prevent the parish from repeating the terror of the Dark Winter.","goal":"Keep Ilyan focused on the lantern rite and stop the council from using the missing page to condemn the wardens.","flaw":"She protects people by withholding the truth, even when that choice leaves them unprepared.","internal_conflict":"Edda believes silence has preserved the parish, yet she knows secrecy has made the wall's keepers look guilty and left the new lamplighter without the knowledge he needs.","external_conflict":"The council's accusations and the dwindling oil supply threaten the wardens' ability to keep the wall lit, while Ilyan's questions risk reopening the dispute.","arc":"Edda begins convinced that a guarded silence is safer than naming the night the ledger lost. When Ilyan's private record shows that the wardens cannot prove their own account, she chooses to tell him what she remembers rather than demand his obedience. She ends still wary of panic, but willing to share responsibility for the truth instead of using secrecy as protection.","personality_traits":["disciplined","protective","secretive","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wall knowledge","description":"Knows the wall's lantern niches, their maintenance needs, and which flames are most vulnerable to wind.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Warden's authority","description":"Can command the attention of the Lamp Wardens through long service and practical competence.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_elspeth_rusk","name":"Elspeth Rusk","role":"antagonist","description":"Elspeth is the Moot Council's most exacting keeper of the lit-night ledger, responsible for entering each night's record and calling in the oil tithe at midwinter. She grew up in a household that paid its measure on time and regards a reliable record as the parish's only defense against fear and accusation. Tall and sharply dressed in dark wool, she keeps her sleeves clean even in the kirk's soot-stained rooms and uses a fine hand to make each ledger line look indisputable. Her insistence on order has become a shield against any fact she cannot control.","home_location_id":"loc_moot_kirk","faction_id":"fac_moot_council","motivation":"Preserve the council's authority over the ledger and the collection of oil tithes.","goal":"Secure enough oil for the wall and prevent the missing page from becoming grounds to dismiss the council's records.","flaw":"She treats uncertainty as a threat to be managed and uses procedure to silence inconvenient testimony.","internal_conflict":"Elspeth fears that admitting the ledger is incomplete will undo the order she has built her life around, but defending it too fiercely risks making the council's silence look like guilt.","external_conflict":"Ilyan's observations and the turf-cutters' challenge to the oil count threaten the council's account of the missing night and its authority to call in the tithe.","arc":"Elspeth begins certain that a flawless ledger is more important than the testimony of frightened or resentful parishioners. When Ilyan's record conflicts with the council's account and the wall's oil runs short, she must choose whether to suppress his evidence or open the tithe count to scrutiny. She ends by allowing the dispute to be recorded openly, accepting a loss of control rather than turning an incomplete record into a false certainty.","personality_traits":["precise","commanding","calculating","uneasy with uncertainty"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger keeping","description":"Maintains precise entries and can identify discrepancies in tallies and written records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Council persuasion","description":"Frames decisions in terms of parish duty and can steer a council meeting toward her preferred procedure.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_noll_sayer","name":"Noll Sayer","role":"supporting","description":"A turf-cutter from the families who work the Bog Hollow, Noll knows the peat cuttings by their smell, sound, and treacherous give underfoot. He has paid the household oil tithe for years and believes the wardens count more oil than the wall ever receives. Broad and weather-darkened, with a limp from a hidden peat sink, he carries no lamp beyond the bog line after dusk, even when the walk home is dangerous. His bluntness is partly anger and partly a refusal to pretend that the parish's rules cost everyone equally.","home_location_id":"loc_bog_hollow","faction_id":"fac_turf_cutters","motivation":"Protect the turf-cutters from being blamed for a shortfall caused by the council's or wardens' accounting.","goal":"Make the oil count visible before midwinter so his family is not forced to pay a tithe they cannot afford.","flaw":"His suspicion makes him reject help from anyone associated with the council or wardens, even when cooperation could protect the cutters.","internal_conflict":"Noll wants the parish to honor its obligations to the families who supply the oil, but he fears that speaking openly will bring the council's attention down on them.","external_conflict":"The oil tithe is being called in despite the turf-cutters' claim that the wardens over-count it, and the missing ledger page makes the true balance impossible to check.","arc":"Noll begins determined to refuse the council's demand and keep the cutters' account separate from the wardens' claims. When Ilyan asks him to compare the household measures with the wall's actual oil needs, Noll chooses to bring the cutters' tally to the Moot Kirk rather than keep his evidence private. He ends prepared to bargain openly with the council, having confronted his habit of treating every request as a trap.","personality_traits":["plain-spoken","suspicious","resourceful","loyal to family"],"abilities":[{"name":"Peatland sense","description":"Reads the bog's firmness, water, and sound well enough to work the cuttings cautiously.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Tithe tally","description":"Keeps a practical household account of oil measures and can challenge a count that does not match what was delivered.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilyan_edda","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","target_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Edda Marr trains Ilyan Vey in the wall's lantern rite, but her habit of withholding what she knows about the missing page makes her guidance a source of mistrust."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_elspeth","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","target_character_id":"chr_elspeth_rusk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ilyan Vey needs Elspeth Rusk's ledger to learn which night is missing, while Elspeth treats his independent observations as a challenge to the council's authority."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_noll","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","target_character_id":"chr_noll_sayer","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilyan Vey and Noll Sayer compare the wall's oil needs with the turf-cutters' tithe tally, though Noll doubts that a new warden can be trusted."},{"id":"rel_edda_elspeth","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","target_character_id":"chr_elspeth_rusk","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Edda Marr blames Elspeth Rusk's council for using the incomplete ledger to accuse the wardens, while Elspeth suspects Edda is hiding the truth about the missing night."},{"id":"rel_noll_edda","source_character_id":"chr_noll_sayer","target_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Noll Sayer believes Edda Marr's wardens over-count the oil they receive, while Edda sees his refusal to trust their tally as a threat to the wall's upkeep."}]}
