n the testimony of frightened or resentful parishioners. When Ilyan's record conflicts with the council's account and the wall's oil runs short, she must choose whether to suppress his evidence or open the tithe count to scrutiny. She ends by allowing the dispute to be recorded openly, accepting a loss of control rather than turning an incomplete record into a false certainty.","personality_traits":["precise","commanding","calculating","uneasy with uncertainty"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger keeping","description":"Maintains precise entries and can identify discrepancies in tallies and written records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Council persuasion","description":"Frames decisions in terms of parish duty and can steer a council meeting toward her preferred procedure.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_noll_sayer","name":"Noll Sayer","role":"supporting","description":"A turf-cutter from the families who work the Bog Hollow, Noll knows the peat cuttings by their smell, sound, and treacherous give underfoot. He has paid the household oil tithe for years and believes the wardens count more oil than the wall ever receives. Broad and weather-darkened, with a limp from a hidden peat sink, he carries no lamp beyond the bog line after dusk, even when the walk home is dangerous. His bluntness is partly anger and partly a refusal to pretend that the parish's rules cost everyone equally.","home_location_id":"loc_bog_hollow","faction_id":"fac_turf_cutters","motivation":"Protect the turf-cutters from being blamed for a shortfall caused by the council's or wardens' accounting.","goal":"Make the oil count visible before midwinter so his family is not forced to pay a tithe they cannot afford.","flaw":"His suspicion makes him reject help from anyone associated with the council or wardens, even when cooperation could protect the cutters.","internal_conflict":"Noll wants the parish to honor its obligations to the families who supply the oil, but he fears that speaking openly will bring the council's attention down on them.","external_conflict":"The oil tithe is being called in despite the turf-cutters' claim that the wardens over-count it, and the missing ledger page makes the true balance impossible to check.","arc":"Noll begins determined to refuse the council's demand and keep the cutters' account separate from the wardens' claims. When Ilyan asks him to compare the household measures with the wall's actual oil needs, Noll chooses to bring the cutters' tally to the Moot Kirk rather than keep his evidence private. He ends prepared to bargain openly with the council, having confronted his habit of treating every request as a trap.","personality_traits":["plain-spoken","suspicious","resourceful","loyal to family"],"abilities":[{"name":"Peatland sense","description":"Reads the bog's firmness, water, and sound well enough to work the cuttings cautiously.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Tithe tally","description":"Keeps a practical household account of oil measures and can challenge a count that does not match what was delivered.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilyan_edda","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","target_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Edda Marr trains Ilyan Vey in the wall's lantern rite, but her habit of withholding what she knows about the missing page makes her guidance a source of mistrust."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_elspeth","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","target_character_id":"chr_elspeth_rusk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ilyan Vey needs Elspeth Rusk's ledger to learn which night is missing, while Elspeth treats his independent observations as a challenge to the council's authority."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_noll","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","target_character_id":"chr_noll_sayer","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilyan Vey and Noll Sayer compare the wall's oil needs with the turf-cutters' tithe tally, though Noll doubts that a new warden can be trusted."},{"id":"rel_edda_elspeth","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","target_character_id":"chr_elspeth_rusk","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Edda Marr blames Elspeth Rusk's council for using the incomplete ledger to accuse the wardens, while Elspeth suspects Edda is hiding the truth about the missing night."},{"id":"rel_noll_edda","source_character_id":"chr_noll_sayer","target_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Noll Sayer believes Edda Marr's wardens over-count the oil they receive, while Edda sees his refusal to trust their tally as a threat to the wall's upkeep."}]}
