ng the council's attention down on them.","external_conflict":"The oil tithe is being called in despite the turf-cutters' claim that the wardens over-count it, and the missing ledger page makes the true balance impossible to check.","arc":"Noll begins determined to refuse the council's demand and keep the cutters' account separate from the wardens' claims. When Ilyan asks him to compare the household measures with the wall's actual oil needs, Noll chooses to bring the cutters' tally to the Moot Kirk rather than keep his evidence private. He ends prepared to bargain openly with the council, having confronted his habit of treating every request as a trap.","personality_traits":["plain-spoken","suspicious","resourceful","loyal to family"],"abilities":[{"name":"Peatland sense","description":"Reads the bog's firmness, water, and sound well enough to work the cuttings cautiously.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Tithe tally","description":"Keeps a practical household account of oil measures and can challenge a count that does not match what was delivered.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilyan_edda","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","target_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Edda Marr trains Ilyan Vey in the wall's lantern rite, but her habit of withholding what she knows about the missing page makes her guidance a source of mistrust."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_elspeth","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","target_character_id":"chr_elspeth_rusk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ilyan Vey needs Elspeth Rusk's ledger to learn which night is missing, while Elspeth treats his independent observations as a challenge to the council's authority."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_noll","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_vey","target_character_id":"chr_noll_sayer","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilyan Vey and Noll Sayer compare the wall's oil needs with the turf-cutters' tithe tally, though Noll doubts that a new warden can be trusted."},{"id":"rel_edda_elspeth","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","target_character_id":"chr_elspeth_rusk","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Edda Marr blames Elspeth Rusk's council for using the incomplete ledger to accuse the wardens, while Elspeth suspects Edda is hiding the truth about the missing night."},{"id":"rel_noll_edda","source_character_id":"chr_noll_sayer","target_character_id":"chr_edda_marr","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Noll Sayer believes Edda Marr's wardens over-count the oil they receive, while Edda sees his refusal to trust their tally as a threat to the wall's upkeep."}]}
